                <pb facs="0736" n="726" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg726"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">834.01/40: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Paraguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Howard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Asunción</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-08-18T11:00:00-04:00">August 18, 1937—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 1:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>25. Department’s 12, August 17, 6 p.m. Meeting not in a body, diplomats called at
                    various times between 4:30 and 6 o’clock. Failing instructions I did not call.
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs stated that the government is returning to the
                    constitution of 1870 and that international obligations will be respected.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Howard</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
